WEBVTT

00:18:27.454 --> 00:18:31.663
For me, it's really been the diversity
of experiences that I've been able to

00:18:31.663 --> 00:18:33.496
have. I've had a series of careers

00:18:33.829 --> 00:18:37.746
at every step of his journey. He's
made time to keep opening doors.

00:18:38.163 --> 00:18:41.246
I view it as a real responsibility,
not just because of my day job,

00:18:41.246 --> 00:18:44.121
but I just feel like it's a fundamental
responsibility that I have.

00:18:44.454 --> 00:18:47.329
Being a mentor doesn't just bring
satisfaction and meaning.

00:18:47.871 --> 00:18:50.621
Research reveals that he can have
surprising career benefits.

00:18:51.246 --> 00:18:54.371
People who spend time mentoring others
are more likely to get promoted,

00:18:54.788 --> 00:18:57.038
in part because mentoring
helps them develop

00:18:57.038 --> 00:18:58.996
and demonstrate their leadership skills.

00:18:59.538 --> 00:19:02.163
So there is a collegiality
to the culture here.